 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "The Hernandez family and the Higgins family went trick-or-treating together for Halloween last year. They returned with 313 pieces of candy, which they will now apportion to the families. The Hernandez family has three children and the Higgins family has four children.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 544689,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Identify the states, seats, house size, state population, and total population in this apportionment scenario.\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The states are the recipients of the apportioned resource (the Hernandez family and the Higgins family).</p>\n<p>The seats are the units of the resource being apportioned (the pieces of candy).</p>\n<p>The house size is the total number of seats to be apportioned (the 313 pieces of candy).</p>\n<p>The state population is the measurement of the state’s size (the size of the two families, which is three in the Hernandez family and four in the Higgins family).</p>\n<p>The total population is the sum of the state populations <span data-math=\"{\\text{(3  +  4  =  7)}}\"></span>.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The states are the Hernandez family and the Higgins family. The seats are the pieces of candy. The house size is 313. The state populations are three in the Hernandez family and four in the Higgins family. The total population is 7."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 544690,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Describe the ratio the standard divisor represents in this scenario and calculate the standard divisor to four decimal places.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The standard divisor is the total population divided by the house size.</p>\n<p>In this scenario, the total population is the number of children in the two families (7).</p>\n<p>The house size is the number of pieces of candy (313).</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{7}{{313}} \\approx 0.0224\"></span> children per piece of candy.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The standard divisor is the ratio of the number of children to the number of pieces of candy. 0.0224 children per piece of candy."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
